<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <title>Heralds Research System · HRS v1.5</title>
  <%- include("partials/metadata") %>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>

<body class="hrs-site-page">
  <%- include("partials/header") %>

  <main>
    <section class="hrs-hero">
      <div class="hrs-hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <div class="hrs-hero-inner">
        <img class="hrs-stamp" src="/images/lionsbell-stamp.png" alt="Order of the Lion's Bell">

        <p class="hrs-kicker">ORDER OF THE LION'S BELL · DIGITAL SYSTEM</p>
        <h1 class="hrs-title">HERALDS<br>RESEARCH SYSTEM</h1>
        <p class="hrs-version">HRS · VERSION 1.5 · UNIVERSAL ACCESS</p>

        <p class="hrs-intro">
          The research, archival, correspondence and formation system of the Order.
          Enter HRS in the browser, install the web application, or use the native
          Android client. Every client reaches the same HRS identity and record.
        </p>

        <div class="hrs-entry-box">
          <p class="hrs-entry-label"><%= user ? 'IDENTITY RECOGNIZED' : 'ENTER THROUGH ONE IDENTITY' %></p>

          <% if (user) { %>
            <p class="hrs-entry-member"><%= user.registryLabel || user.displayName || user.memberCode %></p>
            <a class="hrs-action hrs-action-primary" href="/hrs/open">
              OPEN HRS WEB <span>›</span>
            </a>
            <a class="hrs-entry-secondary" href="/profile">VIEW MY ORDER RECORD</a>
          <% } else { %>
            <div class="hrs-entry-actions">
              <a class="hrs-action hrs-action-primary" href="/login?next=%2Fapp%2F">
                SIGN IN TO HRS <span>›</span>
              </a>
              <a class="hrs-action" href="/register?next=%2Fapp%2F">
                CREATE SEEKER ACCOUNT <span>›</span>
              </a>
            </div>
            <p class="hrs-entry-note">Registration opens a Seeker identity. It is not initiation or internal membership.</p>
          <% } %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="hrs-section hrs-client-section">
      <div class="hrs-section-inner">
        <p class="hrs-kicker">CHOOSE YOUR CLIENT</p>
        <h2>ONE HRS · THREE WAYS IN</h2>
        <div class="hrs-rule"></div>

        <div class="hrs-platform-grid">
          <article class="hrs-platform-card hrs-platform-featured">
            <span class="hrs-platform-number">I</span>
            <p class="hrs-platform-kicker">WEB · PWA</p>
            <h3>HRS IN THE BROWSER</h3>
            <p>
              The complete HRS client at <strong>heraldsofthelion.org/app/</strong>.
              On supported devices it can be installed to the home screen and opened
              in standalone mode.
            </p>
            <a class="hrs-platform-button" href="<%= user ? '/hrs/open' : '/login?next=%2Fapp%2F' %>">
              <%= user ? 'OPEN WEB HRS' : 'SIGN IN & OPEN' %> <span>›</span>
            </a>
          </article>

          <article class="hrs-platform-card">
            <span class="hrs-platform-number">II</span>
            <p class="hrs-platform-kicker">ANDROID</p>
            <h3>NATIVE HRS</h3>
            <p>
              Signed Android build for direct installation. The native client uses
              the same HRS account, permissions and live research system.
            </p>
            <a class="hrs-platform-button" href="/downloads/hrs-v1.5.apk" download>
              DOWNLOAD HRS v1.5 APK <span>›</span>
            </a>
            <small>Google Play distribution will follow separately.</small>
          </article>

          <article class="hrs-platform-card">
            <span class="hrs-platform-number">III</span>
            <p class="hrs-platform-kicker">iPHONE · iPAD</p>
            <h3>HRS FOR iOS</h3>
            <p>
              Use the complete HRS web application now. In Safari, open HRS and use
              <em>Add to Home Screen</em> for an app-like standalone client. Native
              iOS sideload distribution can be added later without changing your account.
            </p>
            <a class="hrs-platform-button" href="<%= user ? '/hrs/open' : '/login?next=%2Fapp%2F' %>">
              OPEN HRS FOR iOS <span>›</span>
            </a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="hrs-section">
      <div class="hrs-section-inner">
        <p class="hrs-kicker">ONE SYSTEM · ONE RECORD</p>
        <h2>THE WORK OF THE ORDER</h2>
        <div class="hrs-rule"></div>

        <p class="hrs-body">
          HRS is not a separate social platform. It is the working system behind the
          Order's research and institutional life. Research, correspondence, formation,
          archive work and member standing remain attached to one HRS identity regardless
          of which client is used.
        </p>

        <div class="hrs-grid">
          <article class="hrs-card"><span>I</span><h3>RESEARCH ARCHIVE</h3><p>The Heralds Research Library, sources, claims, evidence and structured archival records.</p></article>
          <article class="hrs-card"><span>II</span><h3>CASES & INVESTIGATIONS</h3><p>Active files, submitted experiences, investigative records and formal research outcomes.</p></article>
          <article class="hrs-card"><span>III</span><h3>ORDER & FORMATION</h3><p>Member record, formation progress, chapters, offices, Council records and advancement.</p></article>
          <article class="hrs-card"><span>IV</span><h3>CORRESPONDENCE & THE BELL</h3><p>Institutional letters, Bell Reports and the publication record of work preserved by the Order.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <%- include("partials/footer") %>
</body>
</html>
